    "title": "Brooklyn nightclub massacre suspect cries in court: 'I want to go home' - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Anthony DiLorenzo ,\n2 hours ago NEW YORK (PIX11) — Federal prosecutors released stunning video Wednesday showing the chaotic moments of a nightclub massacre that left three people dead and 10 others wounded.\nAuthorities said Elijah Roy, 25, was one of five alleged gunmen who opened fire Aug. 17 inside “Taste of the City,” a Brooklyn nightclub known as a troubled hangout. Prosecutors said about 40 rounds were fired in just six seconds as patrons scrambled for safety.\nMore Crime News Two of the shooters were killed that night. The FBI arrested Roy this week in North Carolina , and he appeared in federal court on Wednesday afternoon, where he cried and told his family, “I want to go home,” before being remanded into custody.\nRoy’s mother and sister left the courthouse without comment. His attorney said the video evidence is unclear.\n“I can’t make heads or tails of what’s in his hands in the video,” defense attorney Mehdi Essmidi said. “I saw my client leaving an establishment and falling down.”\nProsecutors allege the shooting stemmed from a dispute between rival Brooklyn gangs.\nAt least two survivors of the attack have filed lawsuits against the club, claiming it failed to provide adequate security. One of them, Amadou Bah, is represented by attorney Nick Ramcharitar.\n“When he entered the lounge, no one searched him, and they waved him through,” Ramcharitar said.\nBah, who was shot in the ankle, can no longer work construction and suffers from PTSD.\n“Because of that, he’s afraid to walk into any normal establishment,” Ramcharitar said.\nWhether Roy fired a weapon inside the club will be for a jury to decide.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to PIX11.",
